From 3bd40fb4dc4d9aab1056bd8c25e25bc784a22dca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 06:33:08 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 32/37] TABLE/TABLECONTENT: fix the layout, read them in normal
 builds

Checked with the data end of every table in the corpus (R14 to R2018:
sample_AC1014..AC1032, sample_base, example_r14..example_2018,
2000/TS1): R2000/R2004 end exactly at the handle stream, R2007+ end at
bitsize - 17 - string data size. Handles point to the expected objects
(block header, TABLESTYLE).

- TABLE derives from INSERT in all versions: the R2010+ variant also
  starts with the insert data and handles, then RC, H, BL, B (R2010) or
  BL (R2013+), the table content, the table style handle, BS, 3BD and
  the break data (ODA spec 20.4.96.2, ACadSharp readTableEntity).
- TABLECONTENT (20.4.97): columns have a custom data collection, the
  cell style id and a BD width; cells have their own cell style
  overrides; row height is BD; the table cell style overrides come
  before the merged ranges; one cell geometry if the geometry flags are
  non-zero; the table style handle at the end.
- Pre-R2010 cells: the text string only before R2007 and only if the
  344 handle is 0; block cells have a has-attdefs bit and a BS count;
  the has-override bit is common to both cell types; cell alignment is
  BS, not RS; 0x10 is its own text style handle; the R2007 BL + value
  is present for every cell; no extra handles after table override
  bits 0x2000 and 0x40000; header suppressed is not stored; num_owned
  only with attribs (as INSERT).
- 20.4.99 value: empty only with flags bit 0x01 (not 0x03). Since R2007
  a string (and kGeneral) value is a BL byte count plus UTF-16LE bytes
  in the data stream, not a TV.
- The generic REPEAT size check rejected the pre-R2010 cells (sizeof of
  the struct vs. available bits); use an explicit 21 bits per cell.
- Move TABLE and TABLECONTENT from DEBUGGING to UNSTABLE (classes.inc,
  objects.in/.c, dwg.h, dwg_api), dynapi.c updated by hand.
- strrplc: allocate by length; the nested table field names are longer
  than 80 chars and the -v3+ trace aborted on an assert.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
